solve their business problems.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:32.380
So this is just a short snippet
of the lots of different needs.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.820
We're going to touch on
some of these use cases,

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:41.650
but it's already too long to go
one by one in this talk, right?

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:49.020
And to unlock these
use cases, people

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:54.300
need great tool sets that
anyone can use and get

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.860
the results fast.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:01.450
And TensorFlow has
been such a tool

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:05.380
to enable people
to actually build

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:10.540
machine learning
solutions without being

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.400
a researcher of
machine learning.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.920
So TensorFlow is, as
you know, an open source

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.590
library that Google
released in late 2015.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.920
Since then, we have been
seeing a tremendous amount

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.870
of support and momentum
from the ML community

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.940
as well as people
who just started

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:36.040
