detect and as low as 5% to 10%

00:32:23.880 --> 00:32:25.270
of the detection rate.

00:32:25.270 --> 00:32:27.870
And with that kind
of rate, pretty much

00:32:27.870 --> 00:32:33.030
you need humans to intervene and
have the check after the system

00:32:33.030 --> 00:32:35.940
returns the results.

00:32:35.940 --> 00:32:40.080
And they created an
automated approach

00:32:40.080 --> 00:32:43.980
to basically monitor
that approval results

00:32:43.980 --> 00:32:47.670
so that instead of doing
the manual intervention,

00:32:47.670 --> 00:32:52.500
basically you can automatically
capture these frauds.

00:32:52.500 --> 00:32:57.450
And they got amazing
80% to 90% accuracy,

00:32:57.450 --> 00:33:01.890
even for the most difficult
ones that had like 5% to 10%

00:33:01.890 --> 00:33:03.330
of the accuracy.

00:33:03.330 --> 00:33:06.210
And they used deep neural
network for doing this.

00:33:06.210 --> 00:33:09.330
And they estimate that it
has millions of dollars

00:33:09.330 --> 00:33:12.750
of impact for their business.

00:33:12.750 --> 00:33:15.270
And the story doesn't stop here.

00:33:15.270 --> 00:33:18.750
And they are
working on basically

00:33:18.750 --> 00:33:23.230
making the system adaptive
by using machine learning

00:33:23.230 --> 00:33:25.500
and basically analyze
the trends of the frauds

00:33:25.500 --> 00:33:29.640
and new fraud patterns
happening and adapt the system.

00:33:32.850 --> 00:33:37.140
Also, SMFG has quite
a lot of ambition

00:33:37.140 --> 00:33:41.130
in terms of integrating machine
learning into their core

00:33:41.130 --> 00:33:42.330
business.

00:33:42.330 --> 00:33:44.880
And one of the future
efforts they are doing

00:33:44.880 --> 00:33:49.650
is to basically predict the
future financial changes

00:33:49.650 --> 00:33:52.380
of companies.

00:33:52.380 --> 00:33:54.630
So understanding
company financials

00:33:54.630 --> 00:33:56.790
is a very manual process, again.

00:33:56.790 --> 00:33:59.200
And it has a very long
lead time as well.

00:33:59.200 --> 00:34:04.230
So every quarter, companies
publicize the financial results

00:34:04.230 --> 00:34:04.980
a statement.

00:34:04.980 --> 00:34:07.050
And analysts analyze that.

00:34:07.050 --> 00:34:10.909
And then after that, the
banks know, oh, some change

00:34:10.909 --> 00:34:12.400
is happening.

00:34:12.400 --> 00:34:17.040
So what they are trying
to do is to basically make

00:34:17.040 --> 00:34:21.420
the process more real-time by
analyzing real-time deposit

00:34:21.420 --> 00:34:26.635
and withdrawal data and
monitor that with the AI

00:34:26.635 --> 00:34:31.780
they are building to basically
predict the performance

00:34:31.780 --> 00:34:35.560
change in the future at
much earlier frame rather

00:34:35.560 --> 00:34:39.159
than catching that
after something happened

00:34:39.159 --> 00:34:43.060
and they see the
financial statements.

00:34:43.060 --> 00:34:47.420
So they have quite a lot of
very interesting use cases.

00:34:47.420 --> 00:34:50.889
And the machine
learning solutions

00:34:50.889 --> 00:34:57.480
are very promising business
activities for them.

00:34:57.480 --> 00:34:59.370
So the next story
is quite different.

00:34:59.370 --> 00:35:02.240
It's from food industry.

00:35:02.240 --> 00:35:07.280
Kewpie is the number one brand
for food quality and safety

00:35:07.280 --> 00:35:09.120
in Japan.

00:35:09.120 --> 00:35:13.340
And as you may know, Japan
has incredibly high standard

00:35:13.340 --> 00:35:14.900
for products.

00:35:14.900 --> 00:35:19.610
And it's quite a big deal to
have consumers selecting them

00:35:19.610 --> 00:35:21.650
as the number one brand.

00:35:21.650 --> 00:35:23.670
And they make really
good mayonnaise.

00:35:23.670 --> 00:35:29.510
And if you love mayonnaise,
I recommend to try it.

00:35:29.510 --> 00:35:33.530
So they partnered with
BrainPad, which is

00:35:33.530 --> 00:35:35.840
another GCP partner in Japan.

00:35:35.840 --> 00:35:38.780
They have a lot of experience
in integrating machine learning

00:35:38.780 --> 00:35:42.830
solutions into customers'
business processes.

00:35:42.830 --> 00:35:49.220
And their problem was to
detect defective potato cubes

00:35:49.220 --> 00:35:51.080
in the production line.

00:35:51.080 --> 00:35:55.310
Ultimately, this
becomes tasty stew.

00:35:55.310 --> 00:35:59.690
And in order to make
very high-quality food,

00:35:59.690 --> 00:36:05.420
catching defective raw
materials is very important.

00:36:05.420 --> 00:36:09.830
And they have the highest
standard in food quality.

00:36:09.830 --> 00:36:14.450
And in many cases, the
raw materials they reject

00:36:14.450 --> 00:36:18.210
are actually just fine
industry standards.

00:36:18.210 --> 00:36:21.800
So you can see the
kind of obsession

00:36:21.800 --> 00:36:23.690
to the quality they have.

00:36:23.690 --> 00:36:27.500
And this is an example
picture of these potato cubes.

00:36:27.500 --> 00:36:33.290
And I invite you to actually
detect two defects in here.

00:36:33.290 --> 00:36:35.030
It's pretty hard, right?

00:36:35.030 --> 00:36:38.090
And here's the answer.

00:36:38.090 --> 00:36:42.320
So as you can see, it's very
hard and it's very subtle.

00:36:42.320 --> 00:36:45.980
And also, there are
so many different ways

00:36:45.980 --> 00:36:49.970
that defects can happen that
it's really hard to automate.

00:36:49.970 --> 00:36:52.430
And they tried
using machines that

00:36:52.430 --> 00:36:58.080
cost like more than $100,000,
and they couldn't do the task.

00:36:58.080 --> 00:37:02.280
So they're relying on
good inspection workers,

00:37:02.280 --> 00:37:05.790
and it is a very, very
tiring task for them.

00:37:05.790 --> 00:37:09.330
You need to keep very keen
focus on the production

00:37:09.330 --> 00:37:13.490
line for hours to do this task.

00:37:13.490 --> 00:37:17.850
So they created
something they call

00:37:17.850 --> 00:37:21.170
a worker-friendly
inspection AI that

00:37:21.170 --> 00:37:26.480
achieved a similar level of
accuracy as human inspectors.

00:37:26.480 --> 00:37:28.370
And what it does
is basically, it

00:37:28.370 --> 00:37:32.570
monitors the video feed
from the production line

00:37:32.570 --> 00:37:37.970
and makes a sound when
it detects the defects.

00:37:37.970 --> 00:37:40.820
And the worker knows,
oh, there is a defect,

00:37:40.820 --> 00:37:44.840
and they can pick
up the material.

00:37:44.840 --> 00:37:48.470
And this makes the work
much easier for the worker.

00:37:48.470 --> 00:37:54.020
And so here is the friendliness
of this AI to workers.

00:37:54.020 --> 00:37:56.330
And we have a very
cool video that they

00:37:56.330 --> 00:38:04.640
sent us to show you
the system in action.

00:38:04.640 --> 00:38:07.514
So this is the
prototype machine.

00:38:07.514 --> 00:38:08.180
[VIDEO PLAYBACK]

00:38:08.180 --> 00:38:13.580
RIKU INOUE: And you can see
potato cubes flowing down.

00:38:13.580 --> 00:38:17.124
And you will hear the sound.

00:38:17.124 --> 00:38:19.530
[TONES PLAYING]

00:38:19.530 --> 00:38:23.170
And the different tone
means different locations

00:38:23.170 --> 00:38:25.830
on the belt-- center
or left or right.

00:38:25.830 --> 00:38:30.380
And probably, you couldn't
really detect the defects here,

00:38:30.380 --> 00:38:32.313
so I'm going to play this again.

00:38:32.313 --> 00:38:33.160
[VIDEO PLAYBACK]

00:38:33.160 --> 00:38:37.120
RIKU INOUE: I tried again and
again, and I still can't do it.

00:38:37.120 --> 00:38:43.546
So you can see how hard the task
is and how good the system is.

00:38:43.546 --> 00:38:46.650
And another note is that
this batch is the test set,

00:38:46.650 --> 00:38:51.770
so it has a lot more defects
artificially included

00:38:51.770 --> 00:38:53.130
in the batch.

00:38:53.130 --> 00:38:56.280
So with this success,
they practically

00:38:56.280 --> 00:39:01.920
saved more than
$100,000 per line.

00:39:01.920 --> 00:39:06.360
And also, they got these
results in only six months.

00:39:06.360 --> 00:39:09.870
And they are quite amazed
at this very fast turnaround

00:39:09.870 --> 00:39:12.870
because typically, this kind
of project in their industry

00:39:12.870 --> 00:39:17.220
takes really long time--
much more than six months.

00:39:17.220 --> 00:39:20.670
And their approach is basically
to combine traditional image

00:39:20.670 --> 00:39:24.000
processing technique and
deep neural network approach

00:39:24.000 --> 00:39:26.310
to detect anomaly
in size and color.

00:39:26.310 --> 00:39:30.990
So they did a creative
approach to combine the kind

00:39:30.990 --> 00:39:32.370
of conventional and new.

00:39:35.010 --> 00:39:40.070
And I invite you to come
to see the [INAUDIBLE] demo

00:39:40.070 --> 00:39:42.990
on the third floor at the
Big Data and Machine Learning

00:39:42.990 --> 00:39:43.800
sandbox.

00:39:43.800 --> 00:39:47.670
It's a similar concept
of basically using robots

00:39:47.670 --> 00:39:49.740
to do the task you want.

00:39:49.740 --> 00:39:51.450
And you can voice
control the robot.

00:39:51.450 --> 00:39:52.830
It's very fun.

00:39:52.830 --> 00:39:55.990
So please drop by.

00:39:55.990 --> 00:39:59.900
And our last example
is from commerce.

00:39:59.900 --> 00:40:03.940
So Aucnet IBS, they are the
largest, real-time car auction

00:40:03.940 --> 00:40:07.330
service in Japan.

00:40:07.330 --> 00:40:12.190
And they list 5 million
cars every year.

00:40:12.190 --> 00:40:16.210
And 30,000 car dealers
depend on their system

00:40:16.210 --> 00:40:17.960
to run their business.

00:40:17.960 --> 00:40:20.470
So it's quite a large
scale operation.

00:40:20.470 --> 00:40:24.860
And each listed car
requires 30 photos

00:40:24.860 --> 00:40:27.460
for interiors and exteriors.

00:40:27.460 --> 00:40:31.780
And what they have been doing is
basically sorting these images

00:40:31.780 --> 00:40:34.360
manually, because
the images are very

00:40:34.360 --> 00:40:36.970
important for these
listings, and they

00:40:36.970 --> 00:40:38.140
need to make this right.

00:40:38.140 --> 00:40:42.160
And this takes like
five minutes per car.

00:40:42.160 --> 00:40:46.400
And add that up for 5 million
cars, you do the math.

00:40:46.400 --> 00:40:49.690
It's a lot of time consuming.

00:40:49.690 --> 00:40:54.670
And you need to know
what model, what make,

00:40:54.670 --> 00:40:59.620
what year, and which parts,
and what angles are missing.

00:40:59.620 --> 00:41:02.500
And doing that sounds
like a perfect thing

00:41:02.500 --> 00:41:04.270
to do with machine learning.

00:41:04.270 --> 00:41:07.180
So they created an
image classifier

00:41:07.180 --> 00:41:10.630
that does the classification
of model, make and year

00:41:10.630 --> 00:41:14.320
as well as which parts they are.

00:41:14.320 --> 00:41:19.060
And they got to
95% accuracy, which

00:41:19.060 --> 00:41:27.290
is quite high and completely
enough for production use.

00:41:27.290 --> 00:41:32.260
So I'm going to show a
little demo of their system.

00:41:32.260 --> 00:41:35.580
Let me log to my computer.

00:41:35.580 --> 00:41:37.680
So please switch to
the demo machine.

00:41:42.090 --> 00:41:44.700
So here is their demo system.

00:41:44.700 --> 00:41:51.640
And I have a bunch
of photos of a car.

00:41:51.640 --> 00:41:56.410
So unless you're very
familiar with lots of cars,

00:41:56.410 --> 00:42:00.050
you wouldn't know exactly
what year, what make.

00:42:00.050 --> 00:42:08.130
So I'll drop this here.

00:42:08.130 --> 00:42:09.200
So it's uploading.

00:42:09.200 --> 00:42:11.660
And in real-time, they
are doing the recognition.

00:42:11.660 --> 00:42:13.730
You can see the
confidence score coming in

00:42:13.730 --> 00:42:17.190
for each different image.

00:42:17.190 --> 00:42:21.750
And it's now 55%.

00:42:21.750 --> 00:42:26.120
Lots of time is spent actually
on uploading the photo itself.

00:42:26.120 --> 00:42:28.190
So it's getting there.

00:42:28.190 --> 00:42:30.890
So we got the
result. So it looks

00:42:30.890 --> 00:42:35.210
like this is 2012 Toyota
Land Cruiser Prado.

00:42:35.210 --> 00:42:37.820
And they have the price range.

00:42:37.820 --> 00:42:42.620
And also, they have
different angles got right.

00:42:42.620 --> 00:42:44.980
And you can see the
confidence score here as well.

00:42:44.980 --> 00:42:49.160
It's very confident about the
angles and the parts, tires,

00:42:49.160 --> 00:42:52.340
and under the car, even engine.

00:42:52.340 --> 00:42:56.660
So they can effectively
sort the images

00:42:56.660 --> 00:42:58.460
and detect what's missing.

00:42:58.460 --> 00:43:05.410
And it saves a lot of time when
they go through 5 million car

00:43:05.410 --> 00:43:06.810
listings every year.

00:43:06.810 --> 00:43:08.825
So please go back
to the presentation.

00:43:11.940 --> 00:43:16.770
On the approach they took
to build this classifier is

00:43:16.770 --> 00:43:19.090
something very, very useful.

00:43:19.090 --> 00:43:21.480
It's called transfer learning.

00:43:21.480 --> 00:43:24.780
And the concept of transfer
learning is quite simple.

00:43:24.780 --> 00:43:27.270
So you take pre-trained model.

00:43:27.270 --> 00:43:30.480
Let's say, in this
case, Inception v3.

00:43:30.480 --> 00:43:33.570
And it's already trained
on millions of images,

00:43:33.570 --> 00:43:34.710
and it's open sourced.

00:43:34.710 --> 00:43:37.860
So you can get your
hands on these models

00:43:37.860 --> 00:43:40.800
and then chop off
last few layers that

00:43:40.800 --> 00:43:45.840
does the classification
and add new layers

00:43:45.840 --> 00:43:50.430
and retrain using
your own image.

00:43:50.430 --> 00:43:54.750
And the benefit of this
is the base model already

00:43:54.750 --> 00:43:57.690
have learned how to extract
features and understand

00:43:57.690 --> 00:43:59.820
the basic components of images.

00:43:59.820 --> 00:44:03.930
And you save a lot of
time doing these training

00:44:03.930 --> 00:44:06.030
for millions of images.

00:44:06.030 --> 00:44:10.200
And with the new image
set, basically you

00:44:10.200 --> 00:44:15.210
need a lot smaller number
of training data set.

00:44:15.210 --> 00:44:19.870
In their case, they used 200
training images per class.

00:44:19.870 --> 00:44:23.130
So for one car, you
only need 200 images,

00:44:23.130 --> 00:44:30.450
which is a lot less when you
compare from scratch training.

00:44:30.450 --> 00:44:31.560
So it saves your time.

00:44:31.560 --> 00:44:34.000
It saves your amount of data.

00:44:34.000 --> 00:44:38.160
So it's a very
versatile method to use.

00:44:38.160 --> 00:44:41.550
And they used ML Engine's
distributed training

00:44:41.550 --> 00:44:42.900
to do the speedup.

00:44:42.900 --> 00:44:46.620
And they got 84
times faster speed

00:44:46.620 --> 00:44:51.510
using 100 workers, 100
nodes, for training.

00:44:51.510 --> 00:44:57.210
So they got from 28 hours on a
single machine to 20 minutes.

00:44:57.210 --> 00:45:03.280
Again, this enables a lot
faster iteration on your model.

00:45:03.280 --> 00:45:07.900
And since transfer learning
is quite a useful method,

00:45:07.900 --> 00:45:10.990
if you're interested in building
your own image classifier,

00:45:10.990 --> 00:45:15.130
we have a blog post that
basically step-by-step explains

00:45:15.130 --> 00:45:19.400
how to do transfer
learning on ML engine.

00:45:19.400 --> 00:45:22.420
So please go to this
link or simply Google

00:45:22.420 --> 00:45:24.675
"Cloud ML transfer learning."

00:45:28.320 --> 00:45:33.140
So we have been seeing
a lot of examples.

00:45:33.140 --> 00:45:35.150
And at this point,
I hope that you're

00:45:35.150 --> 00:45:38.120
convinced that
machine learning is

00:45:38.120 --> 00:45:42.520
valuable to a lot of industries.

00:45:42.520 --> 00:45:47.890
And I invite you
to really consider

00:45:47.890 --> 00:45:53.200
today starting to look into how
you can use machine learning.

00:45:53.200 --> 00:45:56.530
And GCP can help
your [INAUDIBLE].

00:45:56.530 --> 00:45:59.950
We provide two broad
categories of products.

00:45:59.950 --> 00:46:02.590
One is pre-trained models--

00:46:02.590 --> 00:46:06.100
so visual API, speech API,
translate, natural language.

00:46:06.100 --> 00:46:11.020
And we announced the video
intelligence API today.

00:46:11.020 --> 00:46:13.930
Using these without any
knowledge about machine

00:46:13.930 --> 00:46:17.350
learning, you can take
advantage of the power

00:46:17.350 --> 00:46:19.060
of machine learning.

00:46:19.060 --> 00:46:22.150
And when you want to
build your own custom

00:46:22.150 --> 00:46:26.680
solution using your own
data, you can use ML Engine.

00:46:26.680 --> 00:46:30.010
And ML Engine supports
your whole life cycle

00:46:30.010 --> 00:46:33.430
of machine learning, from
data to understanding

00:46:33.430 --> 00:46:39.500
the data, pre-processing the
data, training, and prediction.

00:46:39.500 --> 00:46:42.170
And as the next
step, I recommend

00:46:42.170 --> 00:46:45.380
you to join some
of our ML sessions.

00:46:45.380 --> 00:46:46.220
There is a lot.

00:46:46.220 --> 00:46:47.585
This is a subset of these.

00:46:47.585 --> 00:46:49.206
These are especially
relevant when

00:46:49.206 --> 00:46:53.510
you are trying to
build your own models

00:46:53.510 --> 00:46:56.120
and learn how to do this.

00:46:56.120 --> 00:46:59.770
